#question(title: [Taylor series not at 0])[
  Write the Taylor series...
  + for #h(.25em) $display(f(x) = e^x)$
    #h(.25em) at #h(.25em) $a = - 1$
  + for #h(.25em) $display(g(x) = sin x)$
    #h(.25em) at #h(.25em)
    $display(a = pi \/ 4)$
  + for #h(.25em) $display(H(x) = 1 \/ x)$
    #h(.25em) at #h(.25em) $display(a = 3)$

  You can do these problems in two ways:
  + Compute first few derivatives, guess the
    pattern, use general formula
  + Use substitution $display(u = x - a)$,
    use known Maclaurin series (without
    computing any derivative).
]
